body:
> > @tejlmand I think we should enforce a convention that module names and west project names should always match, to save our sanity. Agreed?
> 
> As a guideline for Zephyr modules maintained by the Zephyr community, I think it's a good idea to have this as a rule.

@mbolivar-nordic Added the following commit with an extra rule: https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/31156/commits/66e5becd07f0ad1f4348bb3d5d6aec4799a13d87

@ioannisg please give feedback on this new rule. I think this makes very much sense, as we now align how a module is named in `west` and the build system, as well as how to refer to it.

> I also agree with this approach, and I think the way it is documented in the PR is good enough.
> @mbolivar-nordic are you happy with the PR now?

@carlescufi so you are saying you're OK with every module.yml having a `name` that 'shall' match the project name in zephyr/west.yml, even when it is not necessary and the project path would have resulted in the same values? I won't block the merge, but I'm against that; it's troublesome unnecessary boilerplate.

@ioannisg, @JordanYates, let us set the goal of removing everything from Kconfig, and just set everything in the dts:
a. We can't put different partition definitions in one file, so different overlays are needed.
b. We don't want any DT_MCUBOOT, DT_IS_MCUBOOT, ... this means we need to get rid of the mcuboot header in the compilation: just define a partition for the header (the start of this header partition should be used for imagetool), the imagepartition itself is used for the compilation.

The storage layout still may not be 100% in the dts. I have the following for my mdk dongle using zephyr + zmk to get it booting properly with uf2. It may need to be adjusted lightly but the mbr/adafruit_boot partitions are different than what you have defined.

```
&flash0 {
	/*
	 * For more information, see:
	 * http://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/devices/dts/flash_partitions.html
	 */
	partitions {
		compatible = "fixed-partitions";
		#address-cells = <1>;
		#size-cells = <1>;

		sd_partition: partition@0 {
			label = "mbr";
			reg = <0x00000000 0x00001000>;
		};
		code_partition: partition@1000 {
			label = "code_partition";
			reg = <0x00001000 0x000d3000>;
		};

		/*
		 * The flash starting at 0x000d4000 and ending at
		 * 0x000f3fff is reserved for use by the application.
		 */

		/*
		 * Storage partition will be used by FCB/LittleFS/NVS
		 * if enabled.
		 */
		storage_partition: partition@d4000 {
			label = "storage";
			reg = <0x000d4000 0x00020000>;
		};

		boot_partition: partition@f4000 {
			label = "adafruit_boot";
			reg = <0x000f4000 0x0000c000>;
		};
	};
};
```

I also had to add the following settings for zephyr+zmk ; not sure if tghey are required for uf2 but it may be worth additional tests.

```
CONFIG_USE_DT_CODE_PARTITION=y

CONFIG_MPU_ALLOW_FLASH_WRITE=y
CONFIG_NVS=y
#CONFIG_SETTINGS_NVS=y
CONFIG_FLASH=y
CONFIG_FLASH_PAGE_LAYOUT=y
CONFIG_FLASH_MAP=y
```

