@Laczen  Yep, you are right a device will no longer be able to communicate. That might be quite critical in some cases. Obviously, the current timeout-based approach does not work well for emergency cases. To avoid this situation it needs to relax lifetime or security requirements. It is what I meant when I was talking about the tradeoff between the device life cycle and security vulnerability. My suggestion is to decrease lifetime by temporarily enabling to store any stack data asap. 
Yep, I agree that `wise` usage is "enable + do something + disable" routine. 
What I disagree that to keep this routine in the setting subsystem. It should be a high-level algorithm that knows the purpose of data to avoid, how you correctly emphasized, bad security design.

