when test failed, twister let you see handler.log, if there is not that file, it let you see build.log, it is strange. so I create handler.log in pytest_run() function no matter pytest pass or not and append pytest output in it.

@Damian-Nordic, @de-nordic, been thinking about this a little more, should this even raise an error. If data_wra is adjusted to an aligned position at the end of init it does not matter at all. 

I think it is possible to change the two lines just before the newly inserted check to:
`fs->data_wra += nvs_al_size(fs, last_ate.offset + last_ate.len);`

@Laczen @de-nordic 
I tested the `fs->data_wra += nvs_al_size(fs, last_ate.offset + last_ate.len);` code and it works in my case, so I updated the PR accordingly. 
I understand what you're saying about switching from `<=8` to `>=16` alignment and silently skipping `ate`s in such a case, but I'm not sure what we can do about it. Probably the whole NVS would need to have kind of signature/header written to flash, in which size of the `ate` structure would be included, but I guess there's currently no such thing.

>
> I tested the `fs->data_wra += nvs_al_size(fs, last_ate.offset + last_ate.len);` code and it works in my case, so I updated the PR accordingly.

If @Laczen approves the change I will approved but I still think there will be problem in such case:

let N be byte write bloc prior to upgrade,let  M number of sectors:
1) use N byte write block to fill and close 1 to M - 1 sectors and write one ate in M'th sector;
2) perform upgrade via flashing new image that uses 2*N write block;
3) boot the device;

In such case the nvs_startup will at 3) will detect all sectors to be closed and return with `-EDEDLK`.
