If the `pm_control` function could be asynchronous, it should probably return `-EAGAIN` and the driver would later notify the device PM subsystem, e.g. using a new device PM API call. I'm not sure what alternative should be provided, since the current callback doesn't do anything related to asynchronous behavior. In any case, IMO this needs to be removed from every driver:

```
       if (cb) {
