> Do you have a different proposal?

I would say that the reserved-memory node would exclude the memory from the SRAM, like in @JordanYates proposal, however it would not include this in the linker (reserved-memory only "excludes" it). The addition to the linker is done by the driver (if required). 

If the setup does not require the exclusion of the memory (e.g. to reserve all memory in the s, ns setup) an overlay is used to delete the reserved memory-node:

```
&sram0 {
         reserved-memory {
		#address-cells = <1>;
		#size-cells = <1>;
		ranges;

		sram0_ns: image_ns@20040000 {
			/* Non-Secure image memory */
                        reg = <0x20040000 0x40000>;
		};
	};
};
```

To generate an image:
a. for the complete region: delete the sram0_ns node and use sram0,
b. for only the s region: use sram0 (without the delete),
c. for the ns region:  use sram0_ns

