while(1) {
   k_poll(events, 1, K_FOREVER);
   /* set the event in the user object and pass to the state machine */
   user_obj->events = events;
   smf_run_state(SMF_CTX(user_obj));
}

@AndreyDodonov-EH

I initially considered a state table approach but thought  it only useful for simple state machines because of the upfront effort needed to setup the table of events / states and making changes to the table could be error prone. Also, the tables are usually sparse and this would waste memory.

I think the developer will need to have good documentation that describes the state transition that occur in the entry and run actions.

