@edersondisouza Good point, for this implementation I've considered the following design alternatives (other than the one proposed by this implementation)

1. Make tracking another tracing core implementation. While this solution is tempting it would not allow tracing and tracking in parallel and still requires the TRACKING_FIELD object link injection, or we would break external systems that rely on this kind of linking (e.g. Lauterbach OS awareness for Zephyr).
2. Make a separate tracking system independent of the tracing system but with a similar design. Not necessarily a good alternative, this might be a step back and litters the Zephyr kernel source with more hook macros.

All this considered, I agree with this implementation. While tracking does not have to stem from `SYS_PORT_TRACING_OBJ_INIT` (see design alternative 2), tracking and tracing are closely related. The alternative designs are interesting but they come with their own problems.

