@gmarull, we are investigating DTS directions for the longer term but we will still want to leverage this .mex file on the tools provided by our SDK. 

A key aspect of leveraging the .mex and the NXP SDK tools here is that these tools provide a significant level of error/boundaries checking per target board the clocks are being configured for. We are trying to leverage that capability for users who are using our boards or creating custom boards using our silicon. 

So while tests are useful, the collateral provided in our SDK automatically highlights errors in configurations the user attempts to setup.

