@mbolivar-nordic writes:

> As a non-blocking follow-up question, I notice you're using UK spelling here (e.g. stabilise, not stabilize) -- is that deliberate?

This particular word is somewhat inconsistent in this change. Some of the changes, use the US spelling. It looks like Anas wrote the US spelling, unless the context had the UK spelling nearby. Homogenizing to one particular spelling should probably be done, but maybe as a new change. Perhaps use stabilise here, since that seems to be at least the context.

@lairdjm the return code indicates an illegal command, based off the fact that CMD10 is only used in SPI mode (in SD mode it requires the card address, which the stack has not queried at this point), it's *possible* that your card is not correctly entering SPI mode. Could you ensure that you are using `cs-gpios` and not the SPI peripheral's chip select, to rule that possibility out?

Another possible issue is that your card has trouble with CRC calculations in SPI mode. To test this you would remove the call to `sd_enable_crc` on line 109 of `subsys/sd/sd.c`. If the card works without that call, then the CRC check is to blame.

Finally it is possible this card just doesn't behave when in SPI mode. Have you used this card on other devices in SPI mode?

