> API meeting:
> 
> Outstanding issues:
> 
>     1. `typedef void (*async_callback_t)(void *context, int result, void *data);`: Should this be `const void *context` instead so that this signature matches the standard driver callbacks that have `const struct device *dev` as the first parameter?

Happy to change the parameter to whatever folks wish it to be. 

>     2. Direct propagation of `context` to the users of the async framework, to avoid users having to do that independently themselves

I'm not grasping what the use case of this is to be honest. I understood that perhaps other async_callback_t implementations may want an additional context parameter signaling the callback originator. That makes sense! If the idea is to connect multiple async device calls to something like a k_poll_signal or k_sem or k_mutex... that seems like a misuse or potential race e.g.

``` c
struct async_sem asem = {
    .sem = &some_sem;
};

spi_transfer_async(spi_dev, ..., &asem);
i2c_transfer_async(i2c_dev, ..., &asem);
```

What is asem.context when the semaphore is taken? It's a dice roll I'd think?

Why not provide it and set it when creating the asem struct? e.g.

``` c
struct async_sem asem = {
  .sem = &some_sem;
  .context = &some_context;
};
```

Because a CONTAINER_OF can do just as good of a job if an author puts the k_sem/k_mutex/k_work in a container struct to hold the added info. For k_work this is the documented method and I'm happy to document that here as well.

For a further argument on this front, k_poll_signal provides no direct context, it provides an int result and presumably it is not being connected to multiple async requests (contexts). The intended primary use case here is to replace k_poll_signal with a callback and some helpers in async apis (specifically spi and i2c).

In fact the async_signal_cb currently expects a struct k_poll_signal * as its data. The benefit here is that while changing _async APIs to use callbacks and userdata is a breaking change, it is an easy one to refactor today with perhaps a simple sed command adding the additional async_signal_cb param right before the existing k_poll_signal * param when calling them. 

> 
>     3. Deprecation/removal of `sys_notify`, pending a draft commit by @nordic-krch

From my perspective this is entirely optional but I get the idea here that they do similar things, though for different purposes. Less (duplication) is always more of course.

