This is my first pass at allowing failed asserts in setup. It works, but I'm having a hard time adding a unit test for this feature. Unlike Java or other high level languages, we can't really annotate the test function as expected to fail. Since we don't run the test function we can't include a public ztest API telling it to expect the failure.

The update to twister is clean, but there's an issue, the final log `PROJECT EXECUTION FAILED` will prevail even if all tests are marked as passing.

One alternative I'm currently considering is adding a new macro to ztest:
```
ZTEST_EXPECT_FAIL(suite, test);
```

This will create a list of:
```
struct ztest_expected_failed_tests {
  const char *suite_name;
  const char *test_name;
};
```

With this, ztest will be able to actually set the state of the test as passing if failed, or failed if passing. I just wasn't a fan of having it in the linker like that, but I'm not seeing another good alternative. If anyone has any ideas I'll be glad to hear them, otherwise I'll update this PR to use the above macro instead of the twister changes and mark it as ready for review.

