@attie-argentum, what about changing the write loop to:
```    
        if (err == 0) {
                off_t base = addr & ~(ROW_SIZE - 1);

		memcpy(ctx->buf, (void *)base, sizeof(ctx->buf));
		for (addr = offset; addr < offset + len; addr++) {
			if ((addr - base) == ROW_SIZE) {
				/* Started a new row. Flush any pending ones. */
				flash_sam0_commit(dev);
				/* Reload the buffer. */
				memcpy(ctx->buf, (void *)base,
				       sizeof(ctx->buf));
				base += ROW_SIZE;
			}

			ctx->buf[addr - base] = *pdata++;
		}

		flash_sam0_commit(dev, base);
	}
```

The `if (err == 0)` could be replaced by a `if (err != 0)` and a jump to the end.

