> Same applies to `struct llext`'s `*mem*` fields, and `enum llext_mem` should IMO also be renamed to something like `enum llext_seg{ment}` (same for local variables: `mem_idx` -> `seg_idx`).

Would love to do that, `sects` is now _actively misleading_ and the proposed names make a lot more sense and reduce confusion. I actually did already replace it with `mem_segs`; I felt that term made sense with `mem`, `enum llext_mem` and `mem_idx`, so even if better names are available we could avoid modifying those (which are documented parts of the LLEXT API). 

