I have also opted to exclude for formatting the below Error from stopping the formatting from happening 

`UNKNOWN_NODE_ADDRESS_SYNTAX` -> e.g node@MY_MACRO(10)
`PROPERTY_MUST_BE_IN_NODE` -> When property is declared in root of file. Unfortuanly this can be done and by parsing a dtsi file I cannot determine of this is a false positive e.g. dts/arm/nordic/nrf5340_cpuapp.dtsi line 67 includes `nrf5340_cpuapp_peripherals.dtsi` hence can have properties and in the context of `nrf5340_cpuapp.dtsi` it is valid syntax 
`NAME_NODE_NAME_START` -> 3myNode { } as per spec this is not allowed but it has no negative impact on formatting
`NODE_ADDRESS` -> when parser cannot resolve address values e.g. node@MY_MACRO(10)
`UNKNOWN_MACRO` -> Given I only parsing one file I cannot determine if that macro will or will not exists when we reach this file
`MACRO_EXPECTS_LESS_PARAMS` and `MACRO_EXPECTS_MORE_PARAMS` same as above
